</div>
<p>I do have a concrete explanation in mind, but I think the piece works best if you come to your own conclusions.</p>
<p>Adapted from <a href="http://topia.wikidot.com/the-draft-othello-be-offering-for-draft-swap">a self-deleted JamCon skip</a> by <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/othellothecat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3213383); return false;"><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=3213383&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1554558324" alt="OthellotheCat" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=3213383)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/othellothecat" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(3213383); return false;">OthellotheCat</a></span>.<br />
Part of Draft Swap, where authors exchange unfinished drafts and breathe new life into them.</p>
<p>Image by <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Album_of_Paris_Crime_Scenes_-_Attributed_to_Alphonse_Bertillon._DP263811.jpg">Alphonse Bertillon</a>, 1901, Public Domain.</p>
